    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d981">

                <pb facs="1145" n="949" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg949"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.515/7–1645: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 981<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Director of the Office of Financial
                        and Development Policy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Collado</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Chief of the Division of Economic Security Controls</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Oliver</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-16">July 16, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 23.
                    For Oliver
                    ES from Collado.</p>
                <p>Please bring us up to date on progress in controlling German external assets
                    especially in Spain since Department’s 5499 of July 6th to London<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d981-f1"/> and your memorandum of July 7.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d981-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
